name: sim.packUInt16Table
description: Packs an array of uint16 numbers into a string
luaSynopsis: bytes data = sim.packUInt16Table(list uint16Numbers, int startUint16Index = 0, int uint16Count = 0)
pythonSynopsis: buffer data = sim.packUInt16Table(int[] uint16Numbers, int startUint16Index = 0, int uint16Count = 0)
inputs:
1. uint16Numbers: array containing uint16 numbers. Invalid uint16 numbers will be packed in an undefined manner.
2. startUint16Index: zero-based index from which on data should be packed. Can be omitted in which case 0 is used
3. uint16Count: amount of uint16s that should be packed. Can be omitted in which case 0 is used (which indicates that the maximum available uint16s should be packed from the indicated startUint16Index)
outputs:
1. data: a buffer (values between 0 and 255) that contains packed uint16 numbers
replacedBy:
- name: packArray, class: app, file: app_packArray.method
